<description>
Recover the solid marker rectangle from a virtually centered two-axis mirror pattern.

Input structure:
- The input is a square crop of a larger pattern mirrored across both center axes.
- One color is structurally unique because all of its pixels form one solid rectangular marker.
- The mirror coordinate is two cells outside the visible crop, so each known pixel matches positions with row or column index `shape + 1 - index`.

Rule:
- Locate the marker rectangle and make an output grid with the same height and width.
- For each marker pixel, copy the single visible color from its horizontal, vertical, or 180-degree mirror orbit.
- If the whole orbit is hidden or outside the crop, use the transposed upper-left representative of that orbit.

Key insight:
- The rectangle is an occlusion mask, not an object to preserve; the answer is the missing crop of the virtual mirror pattern.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "visible crop of a larger pattern mirrored across both center axes, with one solid rectangular marker hiding a region",
  "transform": "return the marker-sized hidden region; each marker pixel is recovered from its horizontal, vertical, or 180-degree mirror orbit using virtual coordinate shape+1-index, and cropped-edge orbits use the transposed upper-left representative",
  "grid_shape": "output height and width equal the solid marker rectangle"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 30x30 square, always
  virtual_pattern:
    description: a 32x32 pattern with 2-axis reflective symmetry about center (15.5, 15.5)
    mirror_formula: cell (r,c) == cell (31-r,c) == cell (r,31-c) == cell (31-r,31-c)
    crop: input shows rows 0-29, cols 0-29 (the top-left 30x30 of the 32x32)
    fundamental_domain: upper-left 16x16 quadrant, pixel-level random noise
    colors: 7-8 distinct non-marker colors from {1..6,8,9}, no color 0
  marker:
    color: always 7
    shape: solid filled rectangle, the ONLY solid rectangle of any color in the grid
    dimensions: 2-10 rows x 2-10 cols, area 16-100 [observed]
    position: anywhere within the 30x30 crop
    constraint: marker and its mirror (31-r, 31-c reflected bbox) must NOT overlap
  output: the recovered content under the marker, same dimensions as marker
  transform: each marker pixel is replaced by its visible orbit mate via the 2-axis mirror; if all mates are hidden/out-of-bounds, use transposed upper-left representative

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Generate a random 16x16 fundamental domain using 7-8 colors from {1..6,8,9}
    2. Mirror it to build the full 32x32 symmetric pattern
    3. Crop to 30x30 (rows 0-29, cols 0-29)
    4. Choose marker dimensions (2-10 x 2-10) and place it at a random position within the 30x30 grid
    5. Verify marker is the ONLY solid rectangle in the grid (reject or recolor if not)
    6. Verify marker bbox does not overlap its own mirror bbox (31-r1..31-r0, 31-c1..31-c0)
    7. Extract output = pattern values under marker region
    8. Overwrite marker region with color 7 to produce the input
```
